---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://endlessdivegame.com/" },
  { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Survival Guide", "item": "https://endlessdivegame.com/survival-guide/" }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Submarine Survival Guide & Ballast Mechanics | The Endless Dive Game"
  description="Master the deep-sea bathyscaphe survival mechanics in The Endless Dive Game. Learn ballast venting, pressure hull preservation, and trivia trap avoidance."
  canonical="/survival-guide/"
>
  <div class="py-8 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-12">
    
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="space-y-3 border-b border-white/10 pb-6">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold text-[#ffd166]">
        <span>🛡️ SUBMERSIBLE OPERATING MANUAL</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>BATHYSCAPHE SURVIVAL</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white">
        Submarine Hull & Ballast Survival Guide
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        At 10,000 meters below sea level, a single mental error causes immediate implosion. Study the core mechanical systems of your bathyscaphe to ensure your descent reaches the Challenger Deep floor safely.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: The Core Survival Systems -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#0a1d36] border border-white/10 space-y-3 shadow-lg">
        <div class="text-[#4de3ff] font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase">System 01. Ballast Physics</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Buoyancy vs Negative Descent Force</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed">
          Your submarine descends via flooded lead-shot ballast tanks. In The Endless Dive, obscurity generates negative ballast force. Submitting an answer in the lowest 1% of player submissions floods 1,000 meters worth of descent ballast. Submitting a crowd answer vents ballast water, forcing your sub to ascend toward the surface.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#0a1d36] border border-white/10 space-y-3 shadow-lg">
        <div class="text-rose-400 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase">System 02. Hull Integrity</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Acoustic Sonar Shocks & Fractures</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed">
          Submitting an invalid word, a misspelled answer, or an out-of-category term triggers an emergency sonar reverberation wave. Each failed attempt inflicts 33% hull fracture damage. Three strikes shatter the cast-titanium viewport, instantly ending your expedition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: Tactical Playbook by Category -->
    <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-[#0a1d36] border border-[#ffd166]/30 shadow-xl space-y-6">
      <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#ffd166] uppercase font-bold">Category Protocols</span>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white">How to Survive Common High-Pressure Prompts</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#061325] border border-white/5 space-y-1.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-white">Geography Prompts ("Name a Country in Africa / Europe")</h4>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-rose-400">Trap: France, Germany, Nigeria, Egypt</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-[#ffd166]">Trench Strategy:</strong> Pivot instantly to island nations and landlocked micro-enclaves. Submit <em>São Tomé and Príncipe</em>, <em>Eswatini</em>, <em>Lesotho</em>, <em>San Marino</em>, or <em>Liechtenstein</em>. These answers have sub-0.8% submission rates.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#061325] border border-white/5 space-y-1.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-white">Science Prompts ("Name an Element on the Periodic Table")</h4>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-rose-400">Trap: Gold, Oxygen, Hydrogen, Carbon, Iron</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-[#ffd166]">Trench Strategy:</strong> Target the actinide and lanthanide rows. Elements like <em>Praseodymium</em>, <em>Gadolinium</em>, <em>Dubnium</em>, or <em>Dysprosium</em> yield instant +990m descent.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#061325] border border-white/5 space-y-1.5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-white">History Prompts ("Name a Roman Emperor")</h4>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-rose-400">Trap: Julius Caesar (not emperor), Augustus, Nero</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[#8fa3c4] leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-[#ffd166]">Trench Strategy:</strong> Recall the Year of the Four Emperors or the Barracks Emperors: <em>Galba</em>, <em>Otho</em>, <em>Vitellius</em>, <em>Pertinax</em>, or <em>Trebonianus Gallus</em>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Footer -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/10 pt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-xs font-mono">
      <a href="/" class="text-[#ffd166] hover:underline flex items-center gap-1">
        <span>← Back to The Endless Dive Arena</span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-[#8fa3c4]">
        <a href="/depth-zones/" class="hover:text-white">Ocean Depth Zones ↗</a>
        <a href="/high-scores/" class="hover:text-white">Hall of Fame ↗</a>
        <a href="/modes-explained/" class="hover:text-white">Game Modes ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
